+Godot --headless --audio-driver Dummy --path game --script ../build/memory-drift-2026-10-26/test_native_winter_raster_isolated.gd
+Godot --headless --audio-driver Dummy --path game --script tests/soak_runtime_correctness.gd -- --cycles=3 --report-dir=res://../build/memory-drift-2026-10-26/stream-soak
+Godot --headless --audio-driver Dummy --path game --script tests/test_script_parse.gd
+Godot --headless --editor --path game --import
+
+Initial failed instrumentation is retained in superseded-probes/. Other low-level hypothesis controls remain in build/memory-drift-2026-10-26. The first attempt to invoke retain_native_symbols.ps1 was rejected by PowerShell execution policy; symbols were then extracted with the listed direct compiler utilities. An attempted baseline-project symlink was rejected for missing Windows symlink privilege; the baseline control instead uses a tiny standalone project and explicit extension descriptors.
+
+Patch verification uses git -c core.autocrlf=false diff --no-index --binary between explicit task baseline/final trees, then git -c core.autocrlf=false apply --check, apply, SHA256 comparison, reverse --check, reverse and baseline comparison in an owned directory. GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES is set to the owned review directory to prevent parent-repository discovery and subdirectory filtering. Each attempt uses a fresh verification directory. No repository index, staging, commit or owner process is involved.
